---
---

<section id="design" class="py-20 md:py-28 border-t border-[#E5DDD3] bg-[#FAF8F5]">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
    <!-- Section Label -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7A7268]">
      <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#6D28D9]"></span>
      <span>Design</span>
      <span class="text-[#D5CCC0]">·</span>
      <span>Four decisions</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Section Heading -->
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-14">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] font-normal text-[#26221E] leading-[1.2] mb-4">
        Four decisions, and what they bought.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed">
        Each one came out of a run that went wrong. Here is what changed and what it saved.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Decision cards -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      
      <!-- 01: Routing -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-[#E5DDD3] hover:border-[#FCD34D] transition-colors relative overflow-hidden group">
        <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-[#FEF3C7]/40 rounded-full blur-2xl -mr-10 -mt-10 pointer-events-none"></div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs text-[#C26910]">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#C26910]"></span>
          <span>01 · ROUTING</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-[#26221E] mb-3">
          A classifier for routing
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Deciding whether you asked a question or want a refactor is a classification problem. Paying $3 per million tokens for a chat model to make that call is overkill, so Phil uses <strong class="text-[#26221E]">TypeSafe Jev</strong>, a small "System One" decision model.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs font-mono text-[#4A443D] mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#C26910] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>$0.042 per million input tokens, with no charge for output. About 70× cheaper than a frontier chat model.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#C26910] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>12× lower p95 latency. Routing takes under 200 ms.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#C26910] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>If Jev times out, the low-tier model routes instead.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3] text-[11px] font-mono text-[#7A7268]">
          Benchmark: 0 unsafe routes in 50 live runs.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 02: Model tiers -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-[#E5DDD3] hover:border-[#A7F3D0] transition-colors relative overflow-hidden group">
        <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-[#E6F4EA]/40 rounded-full blur-2xl -mr-10 -mt-10 pointer-events-none"></div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs text-[#0B7A5A]">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#0B7A5A]"></span>
          <span>02 · MODEL TIERS</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-[#26221E] mb-3">
          Two tiers instead of six roles
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Early versions of Phil asked you to pick a model for each of six internal roles. That was a lot to ask, so now there are two tiers.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-6 text-xs font-mono">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3]">
            <div class="text-[#0B7A5A] font-bold text-sm mb-1">HIGH TIER</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-[#7A7268] mb-2">Judgment and review</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Architect</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Critic</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Reviewer</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3]">
            <div class="text-[#7A7268] font-bold text-sm mb-1">LOW TIER</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-[#7A7268] mb-2">Fast execution</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Orchestrator</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Implementer</div>
            <div class="text-[#26221E]">• Tester</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3] text-[11px] font-mono text-[#7A7268]">
          Works with Claude, GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek, or a local Ollama or vLLM server.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 03: Security -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-[#E5DDD3] hover:border-[#DDD6FE] transition-colors relative overflow-hidden group">
        <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-[#F3E8FF]/40 rounded-full blur-2xl -mr-10 -mt-10 pointer-events-none"></div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs text-[#6D28D9]">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#6D28D9]"></span>
          <span>03 · SECURITY</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-[#26221E] mb-3">
          Agent shells never see your keys
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          An agent that can run shell commands is one prompt injection away from reading your keys. Phil assumes that will happen.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs font-mono text-[#4A443D] mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#6D28D9] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>Subshells set <code class="text-[#26221E]">PYTHON_KEYRING_BACKEND=null</code>, so code the agent runs can't read the OS keychain.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#6D28D9] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>API keys and tokens are removed from the environment of every child command.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#6D28D9] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>Commands with <code class="text-[#26221E]">&amp;&amp;</code>, <code class="text-[#26221E]">|</code>, or <code class="text-[#26221E]">;</code>, symlinks that point outside the worktree, and mutating flags are rejected.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3] text-[11px] font-mono text-[#7A7268]">
          Four rounds of adversarial review against grep, rg, and git escapes.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 04: Process -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-[#E5DDD3] hover:border-[#FDE68A] transition-colors relative overflow-hidden group">
        <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-[#FFFBEB]/40 rounded-full blur-2xl -mr-10 -mt-10 pointer-events-none"></div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4 font-mono text-xs text-[#B45309]">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#B45309]"></span>
          <span>04 · PROCESS</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-[#26221E] mb-3">
          Small jobs get a small process
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#6B635B] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A typo fix doesn't need an intake interview, an architect, and a code review. Phil picks one of three paths.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs font-mono text-[#4A443D] mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#B45309] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>Questions run against a read-only snapshot. No branch, no commits.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#B45309] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>A one-task change gets one implementer and one review. The quick-path demo above cost four cents.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-[#B45309] font-bold">›</span>
            <span>When a request is ambiguous, Phil asks one multiple-choice question instead of guessing.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#FAF8F5] border border-[#E5DDD3] text-[11px] font-mono text-[#7A7268]">
          Limits: 15 model calls per attempt on the quick path, and $2.00 per run by default.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
